                        "text": "The charges and atoms must balance in a reaction. Silver is oxidized; it's oxidation state changes from 0 to +1. When one substance loses electrons, another substance must gain electrons. Oxygen is a good oxidizing agent for this reaction; it readily gains electrons to go from the 0 oxidation state to the −2 state."
